[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3382255641","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3382255641","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3382255641,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87JmSAZ","user":{"login":"Lucaskabela","id":20960393,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTYwMzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20960393?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela","html_url":"https://github.com/Lucaskabela","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-08T16:04:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T16:04:37Z","body":"cc @bdhirsh @anijain2305 @SherlockNoMad @IvanKobzarev seems to be an interesting intersection of distributed and tracing - marking high pri given our investments in distributed training","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3382255641/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3382387542","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3382387542","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3382387542,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87JmyNW","user":{"login":"ezyang","id":13564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang","html_url":"https://github.com/ezyang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-08T16:41:05Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T16:41:05Z","body":"The most obvious explanation is that the individual ranks are compiling differently","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3382387542/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3387084028","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3387084028","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3387084028,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87J4sz8","user":{"login":"zaptrem","id":1612230,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTIyMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1612230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem","html_url":"https://github.com/zaptrem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T18:35:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T03:19:19Z","body":"> The most obvious explanation is that the individual ranks are compiling differently\n\n@ezyang Since the embedding shape is 1, 1, dim, could inductor's bucketing be sharding it so one of the ranks sees 1, 1, dim and the other sees 0, 1, dim or something? I tried selectively replicating instead of sharding all of my parameters with shapes like these but the problem appeared to persist.\n\nEdit: this was the problem, see below.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3387084028/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3387969946","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3387969946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3387969946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87J8FGa","user":{"login":"zaptrem","id":1612230,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTIyMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1612230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem","html_url":"https://github.com/zaptrem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T01:19:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T03:18:28Z","body":"The problem in the repro script appears to go away when I swap out shape of the start token in the tiny model from (1, 1, dim) to (dim) like so:\n\n```\nclass TinyStartTokenModel(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.in_proj = nn.Linear(DIM, DIM)\n        self.mid = nn.Linear(DIM, DIM)\n        self.out_proj = nn.Linear(DIM, DIM)\n        self.start_token = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(DIM))\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        x = F.gelu(self.in_proj(x))\n        x = F.gelu(self.mid(x))\n        x = x + self.start_token.view(1, 1, -1)\n        x = F.gelu(x)\n        return self.out_proj(x)\n```\n\nI tried the same fix on my real model and it didn't work, so there may be other shapes/ops that cause this as well. What's special about 1, 1, DIM vs DIM that would cause this?\n\n~~Additionally, I got the compiled graph from the ranks and they appeared to be identical apart from different devices.~~ nvm, see below","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3387969946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3388132239","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3388132239","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3388132239,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87J8suP","user":{"login":"zaptrem","id":1612230,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTIyMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1612230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem","html_url":"https://github.com/zaptrem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T03:18:18Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T03:18:18Z","body":"I think I figured it out (I think @ezyang was right): Two ranks call torch.compile() on the same graph, but one rank sees fewer all_gather ops because a parameter with shape (1,1,whatever) is sharded along dim0. The shard length on rank1 is zero, so inductor drops the all_gather for that rank. The bucketing pass then merges a different number of collectives per rank, so NCCL waits forever. Replicating any tensors whose shard dimension is smaller than or not divisible by the mesh slice keeps both ranks with identical collectives and the hang disappears. Bucketing probably needs to guard against zero-length shards rather than silently removing the all_gather (or maybe shard along a better dim?).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3388132239/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3403138228","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3403138228","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3403138228,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87K18S0","user":{"login":"Lucaskabela","id":20960393,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTYwMzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20960393?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela","html_url":"https://github.com/Lucaskabela","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lucaskabela/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T18:38:13Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T18:38:13Z","body":"cc @eellison ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3403138228/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3403200988","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3403200988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3403200988,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87K2Lnc","user":{"login":"eellison","id":11477974,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDc3OTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11477974?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison","html_url":"https://github.com/eellison","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eellison/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T19:00:51Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T19:02:15Z","body":"cc @zaptrem, the bucketing passes are a little bit in flux, and assume spmd graphs. eventually we will have a better user api for this workflow but it doesnt exist yet. for now use at your own risk.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3403200988/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3403857685","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3403857685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3403857685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87K4r8V","user":{"login":"zaptrem","id":1612230,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTIyMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1612230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem","html_url":"https://github.com/zaptrem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T22:49:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T22:49:37Z","body":"> cc [@zaptrem](https://github.com/zaptrem), the bucketing passes are a little bit in flux, and assume spmd graphs. eventually we will have a better user api for this workflow but it doesnt exist yet. for now use at your own risk.\n\nThanks for getting back, I'm just experimenting to see if there's significant performance left on the table with this new stuff compared to our current manual FSDP2 wrapping+compile setup. Even with the above workaround and the overlap preserving bucketer performance seems to significantly trail FSDP2+compile. Can you explain what an SPMD graph is in this context? Docs seem to indicate it's got something to do with XLA/is for TPUs.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3403857685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3404154974","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3404154974","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3404154974,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87K50he","user":{"login":"ezyang","id":13564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang","html_url":"https://github.com/ezyang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T01:07:56Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T01:07:56Z","body":"> Even with the above workaround and the overlap preserving bucketer performance seems to significantly trail FSDP2+compile.\n\nWhen Elias says \"in flux\", this is part of it; we haven't gotten parity on llama 8b yet 🤣 . We're pretty close though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3404154974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3404156249","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3404156249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3404156249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87K501Z","user":{"login":"ezyang","id":13564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang","html_url":"https://github.com/ezyang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T01:08:33Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T01:08:33Z","body":"@zaptrem I owe you a longer explanation but I need to take time to write it up","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3404156249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3404267365","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3404267365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3404267365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87K6P9l","user":{"login":"zaptrem","id":1612230,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTIyMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1612230?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem","html_url":"https://github.com/zaptrem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zaptrem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T02:17:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T02:20:52Z","body":"> [@zaptrem](https://github.com/zaptrem) I owe you a longer explanation but I need to take time to write it up\n\nThanks! Looking forward to it.\n\n> > Even with the above workaround and the overlap preserving bucketer performance seems to significantly trail FSDP2+compile.\n> \n> When Elias says \"in flux\", this is part of it; we haven't gotten parity on llama 8b yet 🤣 . We're pretty close though.\n\nAh, I assumed the results would be similar to the SimpleFSDP paper which claimed to be ahead of FSDP2. I was excited to try running an FSDP llama 8b with full cudagraphs (I got this to work via a tweak to SimpleFSDP that would replicate all the params whose dims weren't divisble by the world size), but not with the overlap bucketer so it was still slightly slower than FSDP2). I assume not all the tricks from their Inductor version have been upstreamed yet? I'm also curious how Inductor would be able to handle FSDP2's multi-stream communication stuff.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3404267365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3475467194","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891#issuecomment-3475467194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/164891","id":3475467194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87PJ2u6","user":{"login":"ezyang","id":13564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang","html_url":"https://github.com/ezyang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-01T02:31:01Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T02:31:01Z","body":"OK, so the current recommended configs are:\n\n```\n    torch._inductor.config.test_configs.aten_fx_overlap_preserving_bucketing = True\n    torch._inductor.config.test_configs.aten_fx_overlap_insert_overlap_deps = False\n    torch._inductor.config.allow_buffer_reuse = False\n```\n\nthis might change but this is the most updated overlap pass. It's not super battle tested but we have done some testing on it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3475467194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]